  "market_context": "During an uptrend in US 100, a long trade was entered at the Fibonacci gold zone (0.5–0.618 retracement) after a break of structure. The DeepSeek AI news announcement caused a sudden ~6% market drop, triggering the pre-set stop-loss.",
  "key_observation": "The analyst emphasized that despite strong technical setup (BOS, gold zone, doji + engulfing candle), the unexpected news event caused a sharp reversal—highlighting why stop-losses are non-negotiable to limit catastrophic loss.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify the impulse move that broke the previous structure (top to bottom of the strongest bullish momentum candles).",
    "Step 2: Draw Fibonacci retracement from the swing low to swing high of that impulse move.",
    "Step 3: Locate the Fibonacci Gold Zone (0.5–0.618 retracement) as the high-probability long entry area.",
    "Step 4: Confirm entry with price weakness, a doji candle, and a subsequent bullish engulfing candle at the gold zone.",
    "Step 5: Place stop-loss below the 0.618 level (or below the engulfing candle low) to limit risk.",
    "Step 6: When DeepSeek news dropped markets ~6%, price breached the stop-loss, capping loss instead of allowing unlimited drawdown."
  ],
  "outcome": "Stop-loss triggered; small loss incurred instead of large drawdown. Trade exited before further downside.",
  "lessons": "Even perfect technical setups can fail due to exogenous news shocks; disciplined stop-loss placement is essential to preserve capital and survive black-swan events.",
